-- title:
--   ℓ-power torsion of Pic⁰ of the Drinfeld curve
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $k$ be a field which is an algebraically closed extension of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ (an algebra over `GaloisField q 2`), and assume that the coordinate ring `CoordRing q k`, namely the quotient of the polynomial ring $k[x_0,x_1]$ in two variables by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`, is a domain. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \neq q$. Write $F =$ `drinfeldFunctionField q k` for the fraction field of `CoordRing q k`, and let $\mathrm{Pic}^0(k,F)$ be the quotient of the group of degree-zero divisors of $F$ over $k$ by the subgroup of principal divisors of degree zero. Then the predicate [`AlgebraicCurve.AbelJacobiCard k F ℓ (q*(q-1)/2)`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L252) holds, that is: for every natural number $n$, the $\ell^n$-torsion subgroup of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(k,F)$ (the elements killed by $\ell^n$, as a $\mathbb{Z}$-torsion submodule) is finite of cardinality exactly $\ell^{2gn}$, where $g = q(q-1)/2$ is computed with truncated division of natural numbers.
--
--   This is the expected count of $\ell$-power torsion in the degree-zero divisor class group of a curve of genus $g$ over an algebraically closed field, here for the Drinfeld curve $xy^q - x^qy = 1$, whose genus is $q(q-1)/2$; it is obtained by combining the genus computation with the general counting criterion for curves admitting a Frobenius-type endomorphism over a finite subfield. It is used in the study of the mod-$\ell$ representations attached to the Drinfeld curve, in particular in the vanishing of intertwining maps for cuspidal representations and in the resulting statements about inertia labels of newforms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_abelJacobiCard_drinfeldFunctionField.lean

